I don't think Excalibur's level drain protection is all that useful.
Wraiths and vampires don't show up very often on the early levels,
and by the time I get down to the deep levels, my armor class is
usually so good that they can't drain my levels anyhow.  In fact,
I can't recall ever getting level drained.   

Of course, the best policy would be to wield one of the powerful
weapons (Frost Brand, Fire Brand, or Mjollnir) and carry Excalibur
or Stormbringer in your pack as a backup, ready to be whipped out
when you run into a level draining creature or a monster immune to
your primary weapon.  Having two good weapons is a good idea in 
case a nymph swipes one.

Bradley


